CaramOS additions to Debian's fastfetch packaging
=================================================

caramos.txt   -> /usr/share/fastfetch/logos/caramos.txt
    The CaramOS logo, a star fruit in an orange circle, 42x18, made from
    config/includes.chroot/usr/share/caramos/ascii-logo.txt of the CaramOS
    repository. Colour slots: $1 the circle, $2 the star, $3 its edges.

config.jsonc  -> /etc/xdg/fastfetch/config.jsonc
    The system-wide default config: the logo above in the CaramOS colours,
    the title in orange and the keys in CaramOS green. The modules are
    fastfetch's default list (a config without "modules" shows the logo only).

Without them, fastfetch on CaramOS shows the Ubuntu logo: it has no CaramOS
logo of its own and falls back to the first word of ID_LIKE in
/etc/os-release. The OS line needs nothing: fastfetch prints PRETTY_NAME,
"CaramOS 1.5.0 Xfce x86_64".

fastfetch reads the first fastfetch/config.jsonc it finds in
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME, ~/.config, ~, $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS, /etc/xdg and /etc, so a
user's ~/.config/fastfetch/config.jsonc replaces this file. Command-line
options still apply on top (fastfetch --logo none, -l ubuntu, ...).
